1
00:00:01,108 --> 00:00:01,070
Twenty thousand.

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:04,550
That's how many utes Kia was talking
about selling in the first year of its

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,430
brand-new Tasman.

4
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:06,870
Fifteen months later,

5
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:10,410
the real number was fewer than eight
thousand and Kia's own global planning

6
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:14,590
boss admitted: "Clearly we are not
satisfied yet." And that's just one of the

7
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:16,670
disasters of 2026.

8
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:21,090
A Tesla that Australians waited almost
seven years for cancelled by email.

9
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:25,030
A big family SUV pulled from
sale after a tragedy overseas.

10
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,510
A famous French brand
dumped by its own importer.

11
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:31,290
An American icon whose sales
collapsed by two thirds.

12
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:35,550
And a Japanese giant whose own boss
says this year is "the low point".

13
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,430
Here's what makes it even crazier.

14
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:41,310
2026 is shaping up as a huge
year for new cars in Australia.

15
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:43,650
October was the biggest October ever.

16
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:45,430
Buyers have money, and
they're spending it.

17
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,170
They're just not spending it on these.

18
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,210
So in this video,

19
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:52,450
I'm counting down the ten biggest
car disasters of 2026 in Australia,

20
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,330
from bad to unbelievable.

21
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:56,330
Real sales numbers, real quotes,

22
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:59,770
and what each disaster means if you own
one of these cars or you're thinking

23
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:01,090
about buying one.

24
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:02,530
And stay until number one,

25
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,750
because the gap between what was
promised and what actually happened is

26
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,600
unbelievable.

27
00:01:07,363 --> 00:01:09,853
Before the countdown, a quick
look at the battlefield,

28
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:12,953
because it explains almost
every disaster on this list.

29
00:01:13,003 --> 00:01:18,773
Australians bought 107,493
new vehicles in October 2026,

30
00:01:18,823 --> 00:01:20,113
a record for the month,

31
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:23,693
and the market passed one million sales
for the year by the end of October.

32
00:01:23,743 --> 00:01:25,153
But the money is moving fast.

33
00:01:25,203 --> 00:01:29,133
Cars built in China were
up 104 per cent in October.

34
00:01:29,183 --> 00:01:32,193
Electric cars were up 237 per cent.

35
00:01:32,243 --> 00:01:35,453
BYD sold more than ten thousand
cars in a single month,

36
00:01:35,503 --> 00:01:37,673
and Geely was up 520 per cent.

37
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:40,893
At the same time, cars from
Japan were down 13 per cent,

38
00:01:40,943 --> 00:01:44,873
from Korea down 23, and
from Germany down 24.

39
00:01:44,923 --> 00:01:47,693
Mitsubishi was down 50
per cent in October,

40
00:01:47,743 --> 00:01:52,333
Volkswagen down 46, Audi
down 45 and Subaru down 42.

41
00:01:52,383 --> 00:01:54,073
In a market moving this fast,

42
00:01:54,123 --> 00:01:56,613
a car doesn't have to be
bad to become a disaster.

43
00:01:56,663 --> 00:01:58,973
It just has to be too expensive, too late,

44
00:01:59,023 --> 00:02:00,793
or in the wrong place at the wrong time.

45
00:02:00,843 --> 00:02:04,853
And in 2026, plenty of
cars managed all three.

46
00:02:04,903 --> 00:02:07,033
A quick word on how I chose this list.

47
00:02:07,083 --> 00:02:08,693
I've looked at sales collapses,

48
00:02:08,743 --> 00:02:11,233
cancellations, recalls
and broken promises,

49
00:02:11,283 --> 00:02:14,573
using official VFACTS sales
data and reports from CarExpert,

50
00:02:14,623 --> 00:02:16,093
GoAuto and others.

51
00:02:16,143 --> 00:02:19,493
I'm ranking them by how big the gap
is between what was expected and what

52
00:02:19,543 --> 00:02:20,553
actually happened.

53
00:02:20,603 --> 00:02:21,403
Let's go.

54
00:02:22,904 --> 00:02:25,305
Number ten: the Mazda CX-70.

55
00:02:25,355 --> 00:02:26,813
The CX-70 is Mazda's big,

56
00:02:26,863 --> 00:02:30,773
premium five-seat SUV, with a
powerful six-cylinder engine.

57
00:02:30,823 --> 00:02:32,633
It was designed mainly
for the American market,

58
00:02:32,683 --> 00:02:36,733
and Mazda brought it to Australia hoping
it would sit at the top of its range.

59
00:02:36,783 --> 00:02:37,933
It didn't work.

60
00:02:37,983 --> 00:02:40,393
In the first nine months of 2026,

61
00:02:40,443 --> 00:02:43,973
the CX-70 sold just 182 cars in Australia,

62
00:02:44,023 --> 00:02:47,333
down almost 35 per cent on
the same period last year.

63
00:02:47,383 --> 00:02:51,053
In the same class, the Land Rover
Defender sold more than three thousand.

64
00:02:51,103 --> 00:02:54,093
That's seventeen
Defenders for every CX-70.

65
00:02:54,143 --> 00:02:56,133
And this is after a big price cut.

66
00:02:56,183 --> 00:02:57,323
In July 2026,

67
00:02:57,373 --> 00:03:04,053
Mazda cut CX-70 prices by
between $3,700 and $8,051,

68
00:03:04,103 --> 00:03:05,693
depending on the variant.

69
00:03:05,743 --> 00:03:07,113
Sales still didn't recover.

70
00:03:07,163 --> 00:03:08,353
Then in late October,

71
00:03:08,403 --> 00:03:12,493
Mazda confirmed that the CX-70 is ending
production for the United States its

72
00:03:12,543 --> 00:03:13,733
biggest market.

73
00:03:13,783 --> 00:03:16,293
Mazda Australia says the
car will continue here.

74
00:03:16,343 --> 00:03:19,453
But when a car is built for America
and America stops getting it,

75
00:03:19,503 --> 00:03:22,753
that's a warning sign for
anyone buying one in Australia.

76
00:03:22,803 --> 00:03:25,803
Mazda as a whole was down
almost 20 per cent in October.

77
00:03:26,636 --> 00:03:29,426
Number nine: the Ford Mustang Mach-E.

78
00:03:29,476 --> 00:03:30,506
This one should have been a hit.

79
00:03:30,556 --> 00:03:33,106
It has one of the most
famous badges in the world,

80
00:03:33,156 --> 00:03:36,526
and it's an electric SUV in a year
when electric car sales in Australia

81
00:03:36,576 --> 00:03:37,706
exploded.

82
00:03:37,756 --> 00:03:42,966
Instead, the Mach-E sold 206 cars
in the first nine months of 2026,

83
00:03:43,016 --> 00:03:44,446
down more than 34 per cent.

84
00:03:44,496 --> 00:03:48,746
In all of 2025, it found fewer
than five hundred buyers.

85
00:03:48,796 --> 00:03:50,466
Ford tried to fix it with price cuts.

86
00:03:50,516 --> 00:03:54,486
EV Central reported drive-away offers
of sixty thousand dollars for the

87
00:03:54,536 --> 00:03:58,306
Select, seventy-five thousand for the
Premium and eighty-nine thousand for the

88
00:03:58,356 --> 00:04:01,946
GT cuts of up to around nine and a
half thousand dollars on earlier list

89
00:04:01,996 --> 00:04:02,926
prices.

90
00:04:02,976 --> 00:04:06,506
EV Central described it as Ford
being "desperate to shift" stock.

91
00:04:06,556 --> 00:04:10,026
To understand how big this disaster
is, look at the competition.

92
00:04:10,076 --> 00:04:15,106
In October alone, the Tesla
Model Y sold 3,105 cars.

93
00:04:15,156 --> 00:04:17,666
The Mach-E sold 206 in nine months.

94
00:04:17,716 --> 00:04:22,886
In the United States, Ford sold more
than fifty thousand Mach-Es in 2025.

95
00:04:22,936 --> 00:04:26,526
In Australia, against a wall of
cheaper Chinese electric SUVs,

96
00:04:26,576 --> 00:04:27,716
it simply disappeared.

97
00:04:28,543 --> 00:04:30,753
Number eight: the Honda Accord.

98
00:04:30,803 --> 00:04:33,853
This is the one that shocked a lot
of people in my last countdown.

99
00:04:33,903 --> 00:04:36,273
In the first nine months of 2026,

100
00:04:36,323 --> 00:04:39,493
Honda sold just 59 Accords
in the whole of Australia.

101
00:04:39,543 --> 00:04:41,013
That's fewer than seven a month.

102
00:04:41,063 --> 00:04:45,873
At around $64,900 drive-away
for the single hybrid RS model,

103
00:04:45,923 --> 00:04:50,493
it's an expensive mid-size sedan in a
market that's walking away from sedans.

104
00:04:50,543 --> 00:04:51,673
In the same period,

105
00:04:51,723 --> 00:04:57,173
Toyota sold 9,471 Camrys more than
one hundred and sixty Camrys for every

106
00:04:57,223 --> 00:04:57,493
Accord.

107
00:04:57,543 --> 00:05:00,913
Honda moved to a fixed-price
agency model in 2021,

108
00:05:00,963 --> 00:05:03,303
with fewer dealerships and no haggling.

109
00:05:03,353 --> 00:05:06,393
It said it wanted fewer,
more profitable sales.

110
00:05:06,443 --> 00:05:08,653
With the Accord, it certainly got fewer.

111
00:05:08,703 --> 00:05:12,833
Now Honda is trying to clear 2026-built
stock with a thousand-dollar gift card

112
00:05:12,883 --> 00:05:15,373
and five free services on the Accord.

113
00:05:15,423 --> 00:05:19,593
And CarExpert reported the updated 2027
Accord will cost a thousand dollars

114
00:05:19,643 --> 00:05:20,553
more.

115
00:05:20,603 --> 00:05:21,393
To be fair,

116
00:05:21,443 --> 00:05:25,273
GoAuto pointed out that low sales like
these are not necessarily about product

117
00:05:25,323 --> 00:05:27,893
quality and the Accord
is a well-reviewed car.

118
00:05:27,943 --> 00:05:31,723
But fifty-nine sales in nine months
is still a disaster by any measure.

119
00:05:32,485 --> 00:05:33,995
Number seven: Maserati.

120
00:05:34,045 --> 00:05:38,635
Maserati is one of the most famous names
in the car world the trident badge,

121
00:05:38,685 --> 00:05:41,895
the Italian V6 and V8 engines, the luxury.

122
00:05:41,945 --> 00:05:45,395
But in Australia in
2026, it's in freefall.

123
00:05:45,445 --> 00:05:48,555
According to CarExpert's analysis
of the first half of the year,

124
00:05:48,605 --> 00:05:53,295
Maserati sold just 101 cars in
six months, down 33 per cent.

125
00:05:53,345 --> 00:05:56,555
Its main model, the Grecale SUV, sold 98.

126
00:05:56,605 --> 00:06:02,755
For comparison, the Genesis GV70
luxury SUV alone sold 570 in the same

127
00:06:02,805 --> 00:06:03,655
period.

128
00:06:03,705 --> 00:06:07,175
The GranTurismo and GranCabrio
sold three between them.

129
00:06:07,225 --> 00:06:08,635
And the range is shrinking.

130
00:06:08,685 --> 00:06:09,775
The Ghibli sedan,

131
00:06:09,825 --> 00:06:14,115
the Levante SUV and the Quattroporte
limousine have all been discontinued.

132
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:17,895
In October, the Ghibli and the
Levante recorded zero sales.

133
00:06:17,945 --> 00:06:21,275
When a luxury brand stops selling,
it's not just a problem for the brand.

134
00:06:21,325 --> 00:06:22,875
It's a problem for owners.

135
00:06:22,925 --> 00:06:25,855
Resale values fall, dealers
get fewer customers,

136
00:06:25,905 --> 00:06:28,575
and buyers start to worry
about parts and servicing.

137
00:06:28,625 --> 00:06:32,665
That's how a brand slowly disappears
from a market one quiet month at a time.

138
00:06:33,422 --> 00:06:35,212
Number six: Peugeot.

139
00:06:35,262 --> 00:06:39,292
In July 2026, Peugeot's
Australian importer,

140
00:06:39,342 --> 00:06:42,992
Inchcape, announced that it was ending
its distribution deal for the brand.

141
00:06:43,042 --> 00:06:47,092
In CarExpert's words, Peugeot was
"dumped by its Australian distributor".

142
00:06:47,142 --> 00:06:49,052
The sales numbers explain why.

143
00:06:49,102 --> 00:06:54,652
Peugeot's best year in Australia
was 2007, with 8,807 sales.

144
00:06:54,702 --> 00:06:58,392
In 2025, it was down to 1,350.

145
00:06:58,442 --> 00:07:00,512
In the first five months of 2026,

146
00:07:00,562 --> 00:07:05,872
it delivered just 373 vehicles and
its best seller was the Partner van.

147
00:07:05,922 --> 00:07:07,372
In the first half of the year,

148
00:07:07,422 --> 00:07:10,892
the Peugeot 208 small car
recorded just one delivery.

149
00:07:10,942 --> 00:07:11,572
One.

150
00:07:11,622 --> 00:07:17,352
And in October, the Peugeot 308 sold
three cars and the 508 sold none.

151
00:07:17,402 --> 00:07:19,412
Stellantis, Peugeot's parent company,

152
00:07:19,462 --> 00:07:23,192
says it intends to "maintain continuity
of distribution in Australia".

153
00:07:23,242 --> 00:07:26,172
Inchcape says it will keep looking
after existing owners during the

154
00:07:26,222 --> 00:07:26,992
transition.

155
00:07:27,042 --> 00:07:30,052
But this is the second French brand
Inchcape has walked away from,

156
00:07:30,102 --> 00:07:35,212
after Citroen in 2024 and Citroen
is no longer sold new in Australia.

157
00:07:35,262 --> 00:07:36,492
If you own a Peugeot,

158
00:07:36,542 --> 00:07:39,022
keep an eye on where your
nearest service centre will be.

159
00:07:40,581 --> 00:07:41,886
Number five: Nissan.

160
00:07:41,936 --> 00:07:45,566
This is a brand that sold almost eighty
thousand cars a year in Australia at

161
00:07:45,616 --> 00:07:47,466
its peak in 2012.

162
00:07:47,516 --> 00:07:50,986
In 2026, it's having its worst
year in a very long time.

163
00:07:51,036 --> 00:07:55,986
From January to July, Nissan
delivered 15,445 vehicles,

164
00:07:56,036 --> 00:07:57,606
down almost 34 per cent.

165
00:07:57,656 --> 00:08:00,106
The Qashqai was down 73 per cent.

166
00:08:00,156 --> 00:08:04,146
And the new-generation Navara ute a
car that should have been a fresh start

167
00:08:04,196 --> 00:08:06,006
was down almost 49 per cent.

168
00:08:06,056 --> 00:08:07,566
Then came the cuts.

169
00:08:07,616 --> 00:08:10,506
Nissan axed the Juke and
the Pathfinder in Australia.

170
00:08:10,556 --> 00:08:14,166
The new-generation Leaf electric
car was postponed indefinitely.

171
00:08:14,216 --> 00:08:18,346
And CarExpert reported that a tougher
Navara Warrior model was cancelled.

172
00:08:18,396 --> 00:08:22,426
Nissan's Oceania boss, Steve Milette,
was remarkably honest about it.

173
00:08:22,476 --> 00:08:25,806
He told CarExpert: "2026 is the low point,

174
00:08:25,856 --> 00:08:28,646
and it then increases from
there on in." In other words,

175
00:08:28,696 --> 00:08:31,606
Nissan itself is calling 2026 the bottom.

176
00:08:31,656 --> 00:08:33,346
To be fair to Nissan, there's a plan.

177
00:08:33,396 --> 00:08:38,186
It's lining up new models, including
Chinese-built ones, for 2027.

178
00:08:38,236 --> 00:08:41,076
But for 2026, the numbers
speak for themselves.

179
00:08:42,839 --> 00:08:43,570
Number four: Jeep.

180
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:45,470
The original off-road brand.

181
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,230
In September 2026,

182
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:50,970
the whole of Jeep sold just sixteen
cars in Australia, across every model.

183
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:52,217
According to CarExpert,

184
00:08:52,267 --> 00:08:58,850
Jeep's sales in the first half of 2026
fell 66 per cent to just 365 vehicles.

185
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:02,350
The Compass was down 84 per
cent and is no longer sold here.

186
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:06,790
The Grand Cherokee was down almost 97
per cent, with stock nearly run out.

187
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:09,010
The Gladiator ute was down 56 per cent.

188
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:12,990
And the little Avenger, CarExpert
simply described as a flop.

189
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:15,150
In October, the Jeep Compass sold one car,

190
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,270
and the Grand Cherokee
and Avenger sold none.

191
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,570
The problem is price.

192
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:22,470
The cheapest four-door Wrangler went
from around thirty-seven thousand dollars

193
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:27,030
in 2014 to almost seventy-six
thousand before on-road costs.

194
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:29,590
At that money, Australians
are buying a Prado,

195
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:33,330
an Everest, or a Chinese
four-by-four with far more equipment.

196
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:36,490
Jeep is now offering four thousand
dollars towards your deposit on the

197
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:37,270
Wrangler Rubicon.

198
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:41,590
And reports say Jeep may use Chinese
partner Dongfeng for future models.

199
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,590
For a brand built on American heritage,

200
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,940
that tells you how bad things have become.

201
00:09:47,617 --> 00:09:49,213
Number three: the Tesla Cybertruck.

202
00:09:49,263 --> 00:09:53,573
This one is a disaster of a different
kind because the car never even arrived.

203
00:09:53,623 --> 00:09:55,213
In November 2019,

204
00:09:55,263 --> 00:09:58,193
Tesla started taking one-hundred-and-fifty-dollar
deposits from Australians

205
00:09:58,243 --> 00:09:59,713
for the Cybertruck.

206
00:09:59,763 --> 00:10:01,593
Thousands of people put their names down.

207
00:10:01,643 --> 00:10:02,773
Then they waited.

208
00:10:02,823 --> 00:10:03,693
And waited.

209
00:10:03,743 --> 00:10:08,133
The reservation portal closed
in May 2022 and never reopened.

210
00:10:08,183 --> 00:10:11,373
Then, on the 23rd of October 2026,

211
00:10:11,423 --> 00:10:13,273
Tesla emailed deposit holders with this:

212
00:10:13,323 --> 00:10:15,313
"After careful consideration,

213
00:10:15,363 --> 00:10:18,373
plans to produce Cybertruck for
Australia and New Zealand have been

214
00:10:18,423 --> 00:10:22,573
discontinued." Almost seven years
after the first deposits were taken.

215
00:10:22,623 --> 00:10:23,673
The reason is simple.

216
00:10:23,723 --> 00:10:26,153
The Cybertruck is built
only in left-hand drive,

217
00:10:26,203 --> 00:10:29,113
and it isn't sold in any
right-hand-drive country.

218
00:10:29,163 --> 00:10:30,293
Tesla is refunding deposits,

219
00:10:30,343 --> 00:10:34,413
and offering a free year of its Full
Self-Driving software to buyers who order

220
00:10:34,463 --> 00:10:40,153
a Model 3 or Model Y instead
CarExpert valued that at $1,788.

221
00:10:40,203 --> 00:10:43,873
To be fair, a hundred and fifty
dollars won't break anyone.

222
00:10:43,923 --> 00:10:46,873
But seven years of waiting for
a truck that was never coming?

223
00:10:46,923 --> 00:10:50,903
That's a disaster for Tesla's reputation
with some of its most loyal fans.

224
00:10:51,741 --> 00:10:53,578
Number two: the Hyundai Palisade.

225
00:10:53,628 --> 00:10:58,271
The new-generation Palisade is Hyundai's
big seven- and eight-seat family SUV.

226
00:10:58,321 --> 00:11:01,411
It launched in Australia
with a lot of excitement.

227
00:11:01,461 --> 00:11:05,871
Then, in March 2026, came the
news no car company ever wants.

228
00:11:05,921 --> 00:11:07,151
On the 7th of March,

229
00:11:07,201 --> 00:11:10,771
a two-year-old child died in an
incident involving a Palisade in Ohio,

230
00:11:10,821 --> 00:11:12,571
in the United States.

231
00:11:12,621 --> 00:11:16,031
Hyundai said the power-operated second-
and third-row seats in some models

232
00:11:16,081 --> 00:11:20,431
"may not adequately detect contact with
an occupant or object as intended".

233
00:11:20,481 --> 00:11:24,591
Hyundai halted sales and deliveries of
the affected Palisade in North America,

234
00:11:24,641 --> 00:11:26,071
Korea and Australia.

235
00:11:26,121 --> 00:11:31,011
CarExpert reported around 2,260
vehicles were affected here.

236
00:11:31,061 --> 00:11:32,211
On the 2nd of April,

237
00:11:32,261 --> 00:11:38,151
a formal recall was issued in Australia
for 2,242 Palisades from the 2025 and

238
00:11:38,201 --> 00:11:42,931
2026 model years, to fix the software
in the electric seat-folding system.

239
00:11:42,981 --> 00:11:45,811
The fix is free, and owners
can get it at a dealer or,

240
00:11:45,861 --> 00:11:47,711
in some cases, over the air.

241
00:11:47,761 --> 00:11:51,071
This is a tragedy first, and
a business disaster second.

242
00:11:51,121 --> 00:11:52,771
If you own an affected Palisade,

243
00:11:52,821 --> 00:11:55,031
check that the recall
work has been done and,

244
00:11:55,081 --> 00:11:56,491
as Hyundai advises,

245
00:11:56,541 --> 00:12:00,781
always make sure no person or object is
in the seat's path before folding it.

246
00:12:01,418 --> 00:12:03,668
And number one: the Kia Tasman.

247
00:12:03,718 --> 00:12:05,208
Kia's first-ever ute.

248
00:12:05,258 --> 00:12:07,208
It was developed with Australia in mind,

249
00:12:07,258 --> 00:12:09,968
and before it launched,
Kia was talking big.

250
00:12:10,018 --> 00:12:12,668
According to GoAuto, the target
was twenty thousand sales,

251
00:12:12,718 --> 00:12:16,488
and seven to ten per cent of the
ute market, in its first year.

252
00:12:16,538 --> 00:12:19,128
The Tasman arrived in July 2025.

253
00:12:19,178 --> 00:12:20,928
And according to the
official VFACTS figures,

254
00:12:20,978 --> 00:12:22,808
reported by GoAuto,

255
00:12:22,858 --> 00:12:28,448
Kia had sold 7,898 Tasmans from
launch to the end of September 2026.

256
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:32,448
That's fifteen months, and not
even half the first-year target.

257
00:12:32,498 --> 00:12:33,968
Kia hasn't hidden from it.

258
00:12:34,018 --> 00:12:36,348
Kia Australia's CEO, Damien Meredith,

259
00:12:36,398 --> 00:12:37,748
said early in the year:

260
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:41,148
"We're not making or looking
for excuses." And in May,

261
00:12:41,198 --> 00:12:43,388
Kia's global planning boss, Spencer Cho,

262
00:12:43,438 --> 00:12:47,468
told CarExpert: "Clearly we are not
satisfied yet." He said "all the options

263
00:12:47,518 --> 00:12:51,368
are on the table" to fix it,
including more power or a hybrid.

264
00:12:51,418 --> 00:12:55,108
The discounts have been huge up to
thirteen thousand dollars off the X-Pro

265
00:12:55,158 --> 00:12:57,248
earlier in the year,
according to CarExpert,

266
00:12:57,298 --> 00:13:03,515
and in November the 2025 Tasman
SX+ was advertised at $54,990

267
00:13:03,565 --> 00:13:09,368
drive-away, down from
$62,390 before on-road costs.

268
00:13:09,418 --> 00:13:10,308
And in Korea,

269
00:13:10,358 --> 00:13:14,208
local media reported that production
was being cut because of weak demand.

270
00:13:14,258 --> 00:13:15,168
Why didn't it work?

271
00:13:15,218 --> 00:13:18,748
Critics have pointed to the
styling and the lack of a hybrid.

272
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:21,428
Kia has pointed to the aggressive
pricing of rival ute makers,

273
00:13:21,478 --> 00:13:23,408
at a time when the Ford Ranger,

274
00:13:23,458 --> 00:13:28,008
the Toyota HiLux and BYD's Shark 6
are fighting hard for every buyer.

275
00:13:28,058 --> 00:13:29,008
Whatever the reason,

276
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:32,688
the Tasman is more than twelve thousand
sales short of its first-year plan

277
00:13:32,738 --> 00:13:34,488
even with three extra months.

278
00:13:34,538 --> 00:13:35,838
That's why it's number one.

279
00:13:36,586 --> 00:13:37,556
Before the verdict,

280
00:13:37,606 --> 00:13:41,916
a few dishonourable mentions disasters
that only just missed the top ten.

281
00:13:41,966 --> 00:13:43,316
The Kia EV9.

282
00:13:43,366 --> 00:13:48,496
A seven-seat electric SUV from
$97,000 before on-road costs.

283
00:13:48,546 --> 00:13:50,876
In the first nine months of 2026,

284
00:13:50,926 --> 00:13:54,316
it found 120 buyers,
down almost 50 per cent.

285
00:13:54,366 --> 00:13:56,636
Half its buyers, gone in a year.

286
00:13:56,686 --> 00:13:58,456
The Audi Q4 e-tron.

287
00:13:58,506 --> 00:14:01,456
Just two sales in
October, down 96 per cent.

288
00:14:01,506 --> 00:14:05,466
Audi has now cut the price of the
updated model by up to eighteen thousand

289
00:14:05,516 --> 00:14:09,616
dollars but deliveries of that
car don't start until 2027.

290
00:14:09,666 --> 00:14:10,016
Polestar.

291
00:14:10,066 --> 00:14:13,526
In a year when electric car sales
in Australia more than doubled,

292
00:14:13,576 --> 00:14:17,656
CarExpert reported that Polestar's sales
were down ten per cent year to date.

293
00:14:17,706 --> 00:14:20,936
The Polestar 4 was down
almost a quarter in September.

294
00:14:20,986 --> 00:14:23,136
Polestar's local boss, Scott Maynard,

295
00:14:23,186 --> 00:14:24,156
defended the result,

296
00:14:24,206 --> 00:14:28,216
saying the Polestar 4 is "absolutely
flying" but the overall numbers went

297
00:14:28,266 --> 00:14:30,036
backwards in the middle of an EV boom.

298
00:14:30,086 --> 00:14:31,536
The Toyota Fortuner.

299
00:14:31,586 --> 00:14:34,936
Eight sales in October,
down more than 97 per cent.

300
00:14:34,986 --> 00:14:38,416
Toyota has axed it in
Australia, with no replacement.

301
00:14:38,466 --> 00:14:41,096
Even the biggest brand in
the country has its failures.

302
00:14:41,146 --> 00:14:41,616
Mitsubishi.

303
00:14:41,666 --> 00:14:44,616
Sales down 50 per cent in October alone.

304
00:14:44,666 --> 00:14:48,776
For a brand that was a top-five player
not long ago, that's a brutal month.

305
00:14:48,826 --> 00:14:52,726
And three brands that recorded
exactly zero new-car sales in October:

306
00:14:52,776 --> 00:14:55,156
Jaguar, Lotus and McLaren.

307
00:14:55,206 --> 00:14:56,096
To be fair,

308
00:14:56,146 --> 00:14:59,376
Jaguar has stopped selling new cars
while it reinvents itself as an electric

309
00:14:59,426 --> 00:15:02,156
luxury brand, so its zero is planned.

310
00:15:02,206 --> 00:15:05,896
But a month with zero sales is still a
striking number for brands that so many

311
00:15:05,946 --> 00:15:06,806
people know.

312
00:15:07,558 --> 00:15:09,988
So what do these ten
disasters have in common?

313
00:15:10,038 --> 00:15:11,868
Most of them made the same mistake:

314
00:15:11,918 --> 00:15:14,028
they arrived too expensive, or too late,

315
00:15:14,078 --> 00:15:17,048
in a market that changed
faster than anyone expected.

316
00:15:17,098 --> 00:15:20,428
Chinese brands moved in with
cheaper hybrids and electric cars,

317
00:15:20,478 --> 00:15:23,028
and buyers stopped paying
a premium for a badge.

318
00:15:23,078 --> 00:15:25,368
And for you, that matters in three ways.

319
00:15:25,418 --> 00:15:28,328
First, if you're buying,
disasters mean deals.

320
00:15:28,378 --> 00:15:31,528
When a car isn't selling, the
dealer has the most room to move.

321
00:15:31,578 --> 00:15:33,428
Ask for a written drive-away price,

322
00:15:33,478 --> 00:15:36,508
ask how long the car has been in
stock, and ask about demonstrators.

323
00:15:36,558 --> 00:15:38,568
Second, think about resale.

324
00:15:38,618 --> 00:15:42,368
A car that's hard to sell new
is usually hard to sell used.

325
00:15:42,418 --> 00:15:43,468
Plan to keep it longer,

326
00:15:43,518 --> 00:15:46,408
and make sure the discount
covers the extra depreciation.

327
00:15:46,458 --> 00:15:49,648
Third, if you already own one
of these cars, don't panic.

328
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:53,308
Your warranty and consumer rights
don't change because sales are low.

329
00:15:53,358 --> 00:15:56,168
Check for recalls, keep your
service history up to date,

330
00:15:56,218 --> 00:15:58,688
and know where your nearest
service centre will be.

331
00:15:58,738 --> 00:16:01,428
So that's the list: the Mazda CX-70,

332
00:16:01,478 --> 00:16:03,768
the Mustang Mach-E, the Honda Accord,

333
00:16:03,818 --> 00:16:06,388
Maserati, Peugeot, Nissan, Jeep,

334
00:16:06,438 --> 00:16:11,168
the Tesla Cybertruck, the Hyundai Palisade
and at number one, the Kia Tasman.

335
00:16:11,218 --> 00:16:12,568
Now I want to hear from you.

336
00:16:12,618 --> 00:16:16,108
Which of these do you think is
the biggest disaster of 2026?

337
00:16:16,158 --> 00:16:17,128
And did I miss one?

338
00:16:17,178 --> 00:16:18,428
Tell me in the comments.

339
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:19,528
If you enjoyed this,

340
00:16:19,578 --> 00:16:22,388
hit like and subscribe
because in the next video,

341
00:16:22,438 --> 00:16:23,708
we're flipping it around:

342
00:16:23,758 --> 00:16:27,228
the ten cars Australians
went crazy for in 2026,

343
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:29,688
including one that's up more
than six hundred per cent.

344
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:30,798
See you there.
